  <!-- SIGNS YOU NEED A NEW SYSTEM -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Signs Your Liverpool Home Needs a Central Heating Upgrade</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Liverpool has lots of older homes. Some have no central heating. Some have systems well past their best. These are the signs we hear most often from Liverpool homeowners.</p>

      <div class="pf-signs" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>No central heating at all</strong><p>Many older homes in Liverpool have never had central heating. Some flats. Some bedsits. Some Victorian terraces. They still rely on storage heaters or gas fires. A full system from £3,500 changes the home. It also adds real value.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Rooms that are never warm enough</strong><p>An undersized boiler. A badly balanced system. Missing rads in key rooms. Any of these mean the heat never quite catches up. A system upgrade or new rad often sorts this without ripping the lot out.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>System takes a very long time to warm up</strong><p>A heating system that takes 30 to 45 minutes to warm up is losing its edge. Sludge build-up is the most common cause. A failing pump or an undersized boiler are also common. We find the root cause at the free survey.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Cold spots on radiators</strong><p>Cold at the bottom of the rad means sludge build-up. Cold at the top means trapped air. If cold spots keep coming back after bleeding, the system likely needs a power flush. Best to sort this before any other work.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>Very high heating bills with poor results</strong><p>The most costly heating problem is a system that burns more gas to give less heat. A new A-rated boiler, balanced rads and smart controls cut bills by 20 to 35% in most homes.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-sign"><div><strong>EPC rating of F or G</strong><p>A poor EPC rating is almost always down to a weak heating system. A new central heating fit is the single biggest EPC boost you can get. It also adds real value to the home. See the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/find-energy-certificate" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GOV.UK EPC checker</a>.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <div style="background:#f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1.5rem;text-align:center;margin-top:2rem;">
        <p style="color:#ffffff;font-weight:700;font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Recognise any of these? Book a free no-obligation survey. We will tell you exactly what your Liverpool home needs.</p>
        <a href="tel:0151 558 0334" class="btn btn-lg" style="background:#1a3a5c;color:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 4px 14px rgba(26,58,92,0.4);">CALL 0151 558 0334</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT IS INCLUDED -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Is Included in Your Liverpool Central Heating Installation</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">No hidden extras. Here is what comes with the price we quote at your free survey.</p>

      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>New A-rated boiler</strong><p>Worcester Bosch, Vaillant, Ideal or Baxi. We size the boiler to your home. The number of rads, hot water needs, all factored in. Every boiler is A-rated and meets the Boiler Plus rules. Combi boilers are the most common choice for homes with up to two bathrooms.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Full radiator set designed for your home</strong><p>We design the rad layout to fit your home. Each rad is sized for the room it sits in. Room size, walls, windows, all factored in. Every room gets the right amount of heat.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>All pipework routed and fitted</strong><p>We plan pipe routes to keep damage to your decor low. We work neat. We clean up at the end of every day.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Smart thermostat and heating controls</strong><p>A new smart thermostat and timer fitted and set up. Nest or Hive on request. The Boiler Plus rules make smart controls a must on all new central heating installations.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Magnetic system filter</strong><p>A magnetic filter catches sludge before it hits the boiler. Most boiler makers want one fitted to keep the warranty valid. It is key to long system life.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Inhibitor dosed to BS 7593 standard</strong><p>The system is filled with rust inhibitor at the right dose. This stops the metal parts rusting from the inside. All major boiler makers need this for the warranty to hold.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Full system commissioning and balancing</strong><p>Every rad is balanced one by one for the right heat output. The system pressure is set. A full heat and hot water cycle is run before we leave. Your system works right from day one.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>Gas Safe certificate and Benchmark certificate</strong><p>Both are issued on the day the work is done. The Gas Safe cert is the legal must for any gas job. The Benchmark cert is needed by the maker to fix and register the warranty on your boiler.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">✓</span><div><strong>12-month workmanship guarantee</strong><p>Every install comes with a 12-month workmanship guarantee. This sits on top of the maker's warranty for the boiler. If any part of our work fails, we come back and fix it at no cost.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

