    <div class="container">
      <h2>How Long Does Central Heating Installation Take in Liverpool?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Each home is different. Here are typical times for Liverpool jobs.</p>

      <div class="pf-durations" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-duration-card">
          <div class="pf-duration-time">2-3<br><span style="font-size:0.9rem;">days</span></div>
          <div><strong>Small home or flat. Up to 6 rads.</strong><p>A 1 or 2 bed home or flat. Easy pipe access. Includes the boiler, all rads, controls and commissioning. Common in city centre L1 and split-up homes.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-duration-card">
          <div class="pf-duration-time">3-5<br><span style="font-size:0.9rem;">days</span></div>
          <div><strong>Standard 3 bed home. 7 to 10 rads.</strong><p>The most common job we do. A 3-bed home with 7 to 10 rads. Victorian terraces. 1960s semis. 3-bed new builds. Includes the boiler and smart controls.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-duration-card">
          <div class="pf-duration-time">5-7<br><span style="font-size:0.9rem;">days</span></div>
          <div><strong>Larger home. 11 or more rads.</strong><p>Bigger homes in Woolton, Formby and Crosby. Heswall and the wider area too. More rads. Longer pipe runs. A system boiler may be needed.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="pf-duration-card">
          <div class="pf-duration-time">0.5<br><span style="font-size:0.9rem;">day</span></div>
          <div><strong>Single radiator addition to working system.</strong><p>Adding one rad to a working central heating system. We do the pipe connection, balance the system and top up the inhibitor. We can often attend in 2 to 3 days.</p></div>
