      <h2>Power Flushing for Liverpool Heating Systems</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Upgrading an old system rather than fitting new? Get a power flush before any new parts are joined.</p>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-orange" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3>Why a Power Flush Before a System Upgrade Matters</h3>
        <p>If you connect new rads or a new boiler to a dirty old system, sludge moves into the new parts at once. The new heat exchanger wears fast. New rads can block in months. All major makers need a clean system for the warranty.</p>
        <p>A power flush clears sludge from the old pipework before the new parts go in. This keeps your new boiler clean from day one. Worcester Bosch, Vaillant and the other big makers need it under warranty. A power flush costs from £350. We do it as a bundle with any system upgrade at a better combined price.</p>
        <p>For a full new system where all the pipework and rads are new, you do not need a flush. We tell you at the free survey if a flush is needed for your job.</p>
      </div>

