        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">BOILER</span>&nbsp; What is the difference between a boiler installation in Liverpool and a central heating installation?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>A boiler installation in Liverpool covers just the boiler. It goes onto your current pipework and rads. A new boiler from £1,800 fitted. A full central heating installation covers the boiler, the rads, all the pipework and the controls. It starts from £3,500. We do both. The free survey tells you which one your home needs.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">FLUSH</span>&nbsp; Do I need a power flush with a new central heating system?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>For a full new system fit, you do not need a power flush. All the pipework and rads are new. For a system upgrade or extension, a power flush is strongly recommended before any new parts connect to the old circuit. We tell you at the free survey if a flush is needed for your job.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GRANTS</span>&nbsp; Is there a government grant for central heating in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Some Liverpool homeowners on benefits may qualify for the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/apply-great-british-insulation-scheme" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ECO4 scheme</a>. It can fund a full central heating fit or upgrade. The <a href="https://www.gov.uk/apply-boiler-upgrade-scheme" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boiler Upgrade Scheme</a> gives up to £7,500 towards a heat pump fit. We check eligibility at the free survey at no cost.</p></div></details>
